{% extends 'layout.twig' %}
{% set page_title = 'Privacy Policy |' %} 

{% set page_canonical = app_url ~ current_url() %}


{% block content %}

<section
  class="mt-16 mb-16 flex flex-col gap-8 lg:gap-10 mx-4 lg:items-center lg:mx-0"
>
  <h1 class="text-center font-semibold tracking-tight text-xl">
    Privacy Policy
  </h1>
  <div class="max-w-3xl text-lg space-y-6 [&>h2]:font-bold">
    <p class="text-sm">Last updated: 2026-10-10</p>
    <p>
      This Privacy Policy explains how
      <strong>{{ app_name }}</strong> (“we”, “us”, or “our”) collects, uses, and
      protects your personal data when you use our website and services.
      {{ app_name }} is operated by Ivan Perovic,
      Montenegro, who is the controller of your personal data. We are
      committed to complying with the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR)
      and respecting your privacy.
    </p>

    <p>
      By using {{ app_name }}, you acknowledge the practices described in this
      policy.
    </p>

    <h2>1. Data We Collect</h2>
    <p>
      We collect only the data necessary to provide and improve the service.
    </p>

    <h3>1.1 Account Information</h3>
    <p>You may create an account in two ways:</p>

    <p>a) Username / Email + Password</p>
    <ul class="list-disc list-inside">
      <li>Email address</li>
      <li>Password (stored securely and hashed)</li>
      <li>Your saved TV shows and preferences</li>
    </ul>

    <p>b) Google Sign-In</p>
    <p>If you sign up using Google, Google provides us with:</p>
    <ul class="list-disc list-inside">
      <li>Your Google account email address</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      We do <strong>not</strong> receive access to your Google password or other
      Google account data.
    </p>

    <p>
      An additional password will be stored if you enable notifications via
      ntfy.
    </p>
    <p>If you enable Discord notifications, the Discord webhook url 
      you provide will be encrypted and stored.
    </p>

    <h3>1.2 Cookies and Local Storage</h3>
    <p>
     We use cookies and local storage for the following purposes:
    </p>
    <ul class="list-disc list-inside">
      <li>Keeping you logged in (session management)</li>
      <li>
        Storing your show list locally if you use the site without an account
      </li>
      <li>Basic website functionality and security</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Cloudflare, which protects our site, may also set a strictly necessary
      security cookie to tell people apart from automated traffic.
    </p>
    <p>
      These cookies are strictly necessary and do <strong>not</strong> require
      user consent under GDPR. We do not currently use advertising or
      affiliate-tracking cookies (see sections 3 and 9).
    </p>

    <h3>1.3 Analytics</h3>
    <p>
      We use <strong>Cloudflare Web Analytics</strong>, a privacy-focused
      analytics tool. It:
    </p>
    <ul class="list-disc list-inside">
      <li>Does not use cookies or similar client-side storage</li>
      <li>Does not track users across sites</li>
      <li>Shows us only aggregated statistics (such as pages viewed, country, device type, and referrer)</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Cloudflare processes technical request data to deliver this service, as
      described in its own privacy policy.
    </p>

    <h3>1.4 Server and Security Data</h3>
    <p>
      Like most websites, our hosting provider and Cloudflare process technical
      data such as your IP address and browser type when you visit. We use it to
      deliver the site, keep it secure, and block abuse and automated traffic.
      These providers keep such logs for limited periods under their own
      policies.
    </p>

    <h2>2. How We Use Your Data</h2>
    <p>We use your data only for the following purposes:</p>
    <ul class="list-disc list-inside">
      <li>Providing your account and watchlist</li>
      <li>Allowing login via Google or email/password</li>
      <li>Sending the notifications you choose to enable</li>
      <li>Operating, securing, and improving the service</li>
      <li>Understanding general usage through anonymous analytics</li>
    </ul>
     <p>
      We do <strong>not</strong> sell your personal data, and we do not use your
      account data (such as your email address or watchlist) for advertising or
      profiling.
    </p>

    <h2>3. Affiliate Links and Third-Party Sites</h2>
    <p>
      Some links on {{ app_name }} are <strong>affiliate links</strong>, for
      example links to streaming services, VPN providers, or online stores. If
      you click one and make a purchase or sign up, we may earn a commission
      <strong>at no extra cost to you</strong>. Such links are marked as
      advertisements or sponsored.
    </p>
    <p>
      When you click an affiliate link you leave our site. The destination site
      and its affiliate network may set cookies and collect data about you under
      their own privacy policies, which we do not control. We receive only
      aggregated commission reports and do not receive personal data about you
      from them.
    </p>
    <p>
      We do not currently load advertising or affiliate-tracking scripts on our
      pages. If we ever add any, we will ask for your consent first and update
      this policy.
    </p>
 

    <h2>4. Legal Bases for Processing (GDPR)</h2>
    <ul class="list-disc list-inside">
      <li>
        <strong>Contractual necessity</strong> — providing your account and
        watchlist
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Legitimate interests</strong> — site security, performance, and
        analytics
      </li>
      <li><strong>Legal obligation</strong> — compliance where required</li>
      <li>
        <strong>Consent</strong> — for any optional (non-essential) cookies,
        which we do not currently use. If we add them, we will ask first and you
        can withdraw consent at any time.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>5. Data Sharing and International Transfers</h2>
    <p>We only share your data with essential service providers, including:</p>
    <ul class="list-disc list-inside">
      <li>Hosting providers</li>
      <li>Cloudflare (security and analytics)</li>
      <li>Google (for authentication, only when you choose Google sign-in)</li>
      <li>ntfy or Discord (only if you enable those notifications)</li>
      
    </ul>
    <p>
      Some of these providers are located outside the European Economic Area.
      Where that is the case, transfers rely on safeguards such as the European
      Commission’s Standard Contractual Clauses or an adequacy decision.
    </p>

    <h2>6. Data Retention</h2>
    <p>We retain data only as long as necessary:</p>
    <ul class="list-disc list-inside">
      <li><strong>Account data:</strong> kept until you delete your account</li>
      <li>
        <strong>Local storage / essential cookies:</strong> stored until cleared
        by you
      </li>
      <li><strong>Analytics data:</strong> aggregated and non-identifying</li>
      <li>
        <strong>Server and security logs:</strong> kept by our providers for
        limited periods
      </li>
      </ul>
     
    <p>Deleting your account permanently removes your personal data.</p>

    <h2>7. Your Rights</h2>
    <p>You have the right to:</p>
    <ul class="list-disc list-inside">
      <li>Access your personal data</li>
      <li>Request corrections</li>
      <li>Request deletion (“right to be forgotten”)</li>
      <li>Restrict processing in certain circumstances</li>
      <li>Receive a data export (data portability)</li>
      <li>Object to processing based on legitimate interests</li>
      <li>Withdraw consent at any time, where processing is based on consent</li>
      <li>Lodge a complaint with your local data protection authority</li>
      
    </ul>
    <p>
      To exercise these rights, contact us at:
      <strong>{{ app_email }}</strong>
    </p>

    <h2>8. Security</h2>
    <p>We use industry-standard security measures, including:</p>
    <ul class="list-disc list-inside">
      <li>Encrypted connections (HTTPS)</li>
      <li>Secure password hashing</li>
      <li>Server-side access controls</li>
      <li>Cloudflare security protections</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      While no system is completely secure, we take appropriate steps to protect
      your data and will notify affected users and the relevant authorities of a
      breach where the law requires it.
    </p>

    <h2>9. Cookies and Consent</h2>
    <p>
      Because we use only essential cookies and cookie-free analytics, a cookie
      consent banner is
      <strong>not required</strong>, and we do not show one. We disclose our
      cookie usage in this policy for transparency. Affiliate links on our site
      are ordinary links and do not set cookies on our pages. If we ever add
      optional advertising or tracking cookies, we will ask for your consent
      before using them and update this policy.
    </p>

    <h2>10. Children</h2>
    <p>
      {{ app_name }} is not directed at children under 16, and we do not
      knowingly collect their personal data.
    </p>
   

    <h2>11. Account Deletion and Data Export</h2>
    <p>
      You may delete your account at any time, which permanently removes your
      data. You may also request a machine-readable export of the data you
      provided.
    </p>

    <h2>12. Changes to This Policy</h2>
    <p>
      We may update this policy from time to time. When changes occur, the
      updated version will be posted with a revised “Last updated” date.
    </p>

    <h2>13. Contact Us</h2>
    <p>If you have questions or requests, contact us at:</p>
    <p><strong>Email: </strong>{{ app_email }}</p>
  </div>
</section>
{% endblock %}